[**BOUNTY CURRENTLY AT $450**](https://www.bountyhub.dev/en/bounty/view/27a47575-ef9f-49d3-9685-c056d6825f9d) and already the biggest listing on BountyHub by far.

**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**

WearOS devices do not work with MicroG

**Describe the solution you'd like**

MicroG framework needed to pair modern, current-gen WearOS devices and get basic functionality - echo phone notifications, provide media controls, run WearOS apps, etc.

**Additional context**

There has been an issue open for over ten years regarding [MicroG support for WearOS](https://github.com/microg/GmsCore/issues/4#issuecomment-2581553597).  That issue and another [more recent post](https://github.com/microg/GmsCore/issues/2444#issuecomment-2691206945) have inspired some folks to post bounties for this feature, but it's buried so far down in the thread it's easy to miss.

I personally am posting a $200 bounty for the MicroG framework needed to pair modern, current-gen WearOS devices and get basic functionality - echo phone notifications, provide media controls, run WearOS apps, etc.

Here are the folks who've posted bounties in those threads.  I'll invite them to post again here confirming that their offers still stand, but all told, this adds up to over $500 already.

@HyperCriSiS ~~- $100~~
@realPrix ~~- $100~~
@NullCode1337 ~~- $50~~
@TobiPeterG ~~- $100~~
@doctorgaul ~~- $200~~

*Edit - Amounts now being tracked on the [BountyHub page](https://www.bountyhub.dev/en/bounty/view/27a47575-ef9f-49d3-9685-c056d6825f9d).

